# This machine's settings. Copy to host.env (git ignores it) and fill in.
# hostctl (which passes it on to what it runs), the systemd units (EnvironmentFile=) and the site builds
# all read it, so keep to KEY=value lines: no quotes, no spaces around =, no $.

# The tailnet name this machine is reached by. tailscale serve puts the pages site on
# :8445 and SearXNG on :8888, and every link the setup hands out uses it.
PUBLIC_HOST=machine.tailnet-name.ts.net

# AnythingLLM's storage directory on the host; its container mounts it at /app/server/storage.
ANYTHINGLLM_STORAGE=/srv/anythingllm/storage

# Optional. How many of the CPU's threads podcast transcription uses at each time of day
# (in PODCASTS_TZ, default Europe/Stockholm): a number for all day, or HH:MM=threads
# entries, each lasting until the next, e.g. 4 by day (fans audible) and 1 at night
# (quiet). 0 pauses transcription until the next entry. Unset, it is 1 all day.
# PODCASTS_TRANSCRIBE_THREADS=08:00=4,22:00=1

# Optional. Quiet hours (in PODCASTS_TZ), when the podcasts neither cut ads nor transcribe,
# so the fans stay quiet: syncs still download, and the first sync after cuts the ads.
# Unset, there are none.
# PODCASTS_QUIET_HOURS=22:00-06:00

# Optional. The ntfy server in the Nilson relay's NTFY_URL, which the egress proxy lets the
# relay's container reach (packages/egress, egress.toml). Unset, it is ntfy.sh.
# NTFY_HOST=ntfy.sh
